  "details": "Holding down the Control key while backspacing lets you delete whole words instead of just letters in most programs.\n\nAs a moderately fast touch typer, in the case of a typo, it may be easier to delete that whole word to rewrite it using this key combination, rather than highlighting the word to then type over it, or having to backspace every letter (up until the typo, optionally).",
